<title>HUNGARY: TABLE - NEW AUTO SALES IN CENTRAL EUROPE FOR MAY.</title>
<headline>TABLE - NEW AUTO SALES IN CENTRAL EUROPE FOR MAY.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>New auto sales in Central</p>
<p>European Free Trade Agreement (CEFTA) countries rose 16.0</p>
<p>percent to 86,231 units in May 1997 from 74,362 units in May</p>
<p>1996, according to a Reuters survey.</p>
<p>CEFTA, which was formed in 1993, includes the Czech</p>
<p>Republic, Hungary, Poland, Slovakia and Slovenia. The survey,</p>
<p>which Reuters issues monthly, defines autos as cars, minibuses,</p>
<p>pickups, vans and other four-wheeled motor vehicles not over</p>
<p>five tonnes in gross weight.</p>
